From 66e9c23fc71f73097675a1e310dc4e0c8bd477d4 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Randolph <randolph@andestech.com>
Date: Thu, 20 Feb 2025 15:54:28 +0800
Subject: [PATCH 52/53] swdtb: modify the node name matching method (#161)

The DTB has a node, /reserved_memory/dma_global_pool0@3e800000, whose
name contains the 'dma' prefix. When checking the node, the code may
mistakenly consider it as a DMA node.

To avoid mistaking it for a DMA node, we should add a check for '@' to
indicate the full name is the part before it.

Fix for the "node-name without an @unit-address" case.

Signed-off-by: Randolph <randolph@andestech.com>
Reviewed-on: https://gitea.andestech.com/RD-SW/u-boot.official/pulls/161
Reviewed-by: Leo Yu-Chi Liang <ycliang@andestech.com>
Reviewed-by: Tim Shih-Ting OuYang <tim609@andestech.com>
Reviewed-by: CL Chin-Long Wang <cl634@andestech.com>
Co-authored-by: Randolph <randolph@andestech.com>
Co-committed-by: Randolph <randolph@andestech.com>
---
 .../common/swdtb_merger/swdtb_merger_fixup.c  | 39 +++++--------------
 .../common/swdtb_merger/swdtb_tool.c          | 26 ++++++++-----
 .../common/swdtb_merger/swdtb_tool.h          |  2 +
 3 files changed, 28 insertions(+), 39 deletions(-)

